Results
=======

| Run | Nonce | Scenario | Retired / stop | #PF / #GP(0) | IRQ0 edges / total IRQ deliveries | UART bytes |
|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
| 0001 | `OD518e82fa574df01c00000b50e00000000` | passed | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | 33 / 1 | 34,801 / 34,806 | 24,092 |
| 0002 | `OD518e830aea36265000000b50e00000001` | failed marker validation | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | 33 / 1 | 34,805 / 34,810 | 23,825 |

Both runs reached the guest and expected stop. Run 0001's nonce line validated.
Run 0002's `guest_markers.valid=false`; the captured UART bytes contain
`OD_NONCE=OD518e830aea36265000000b50e00000001[    2.271034] Run /init as init process`
as one line. The raw `uart.bin` is byte-for-byte identical to `stop.com1_hex`;
there is no newline immediately after the nonce. The fixture
`tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/initramfs/init.S` constructs `OD_NONCE=<value>\n`
and submits it in one `SYS_write`. This confirms interleaving in the captured
COM1 stream; the origin of the interleaving is not localized by these reports.
The marker validator correctly rejected the fused line, so the scenario and
aggregate series failed. The comparator reported four unexplained differences:
scenario status, marker validation, machine observations, and ordered UART
bytes. Because marker validation failed, the special stage4 nonce comparison
eligibility gate did not apply.

Current-comparator re-evaluation of the older vector-count N=2 pair
====================================================================
The saved raw vector-count pair was re-compared with the current release runner
using:

```sh
target/release/od-runner --compare-results work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-stage4a-vector-counts-20261115-a/compare-run-0001.json work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-stage4a-vector-counts-20261115-a/compare-run-0002.json --linux-stage5 --json
```

That re-comparison returns
`matches=true`, with no unexplained differences. The saved output hash is
`3fa9e27b9dd0bc053faa18f08ffab2b3874301434623598b18561eb3fe64f105`.
This shows the old UART ordering and audit-time differences are now narrowly
explained by the current comparator for valid markers; it does not erase the
new run's marker failure or establish S5-07 acceptance.

